Z||000000||87GTBro||11-01-2000||01:03 AM||||I am doing some research to see what it would cost me to have my 86 GT switched over to a V8...  I am leaning towards the Chevy small block 350.  I will be using the kit from V8Archie....<P>Where is the best place to find a new, remanufactured, or rebuilt small block Chevy 350 engine?<P>I found one price for a 350 small block with a mid-performance package at $5950.00.  That is a new engine... I don'd recall the website right off hand.  But I was wondering if anyone knows of a better place to look for a good engine.<P>87GTBro||||reg||1
Z||000001||frontal lobe||11-01-2000||01:31 AM||||I've got a '96 LT1 out of a Buick Roadmaster with 30,000 miles on it.  ECM, wiring harness intact.  But it's way up north here.  It is for sale.  HP about 265.  Torque about 330.<P>If you are doing an archie kit you have to move these over a couple inches, notch the passenger rear frame, and get different axles.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||11-01-2000||06:59 AM||||Check GM's crate engines.Lots of dealers have web sites.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ezsurf||11-01-2000||08:04 AM||||Check out the following site: <A HREF="http://www.sdpc2000.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sdpc2000.com</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||11-01-2000||12:26 PM||||If using the Archie kit you can use the stock axles.  You do not need the most expensive kit.  You will be doing A LOT of modifying of brackets and a lot of inventing of unique parts.  Have a good mechanic help, have a welder available and have a lot of time. Good luck and happy motoring.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Richard Parnell||11-01-2000||12:28 PM||||Forgot to mention, got my engine out of an old Caprice.  The body was shot but the engine had recently been rebuilt. Stock 350 with a cam for towing a trailer.  Lots of torque and sounds great.||||reg||1
Z||000006||HAGS||11-03-2000||03:36 AM||||Would an LT1 from a 98 Firebird fit?<BR>Saw one being auctioned for 2,000 at Autoparts.com I believe||||reg||1
